"""Public explanations and private lifecycle shells. No fixture activity or credentials."""

def build_lifecycle(page):
    page('community/lifecycle','How participation works','A clear path from a private application to human review, scoped support, factual feedback and correction.', '''<p class="eyebrow">The Workshop · How it works</p><h1>A useful next step.<br>A way to close the loop.</h1><p class="lede">Know where your request stands, what comes next and which choices remain yours.</p><div class="lifecycle-path" aria-label="Application lifecycle"><span>Apply &amp; confirm</span><span>Human review</span><span>Choose an offer</span><span>Receive support</span><span>Check &amp; improve</span></div><div class="cards"><section class="panel"><p class="tag">01 · Start privately</p><h2>Ask without sharing your case.</h2><p>Choose the kind of support or contribution. An email confirmation starts human review. Keep that private email link to check your application and respond.</p><p>No pay stubs, identity documents, legal names or case files are required here.</p></section><section class="panel"><p class="tag">02 · Human review</p><h2>Fit the next step to capacity.</h2><p>A person may ask you to clarify a broad preference, place your request on a waitlist, propose a limited next step or close it with a reason. There is no promised turnaround.</p><p>You can request reconsideration of a closed request through your private link.</p></section><section class="panel"><p class="tag">03 · Your decision</p><h2>Review a limited offer.</h2><p>Check its scope, limits and proposed time. Indicating interest is nonbinding: it is not a purchase, signed contract, assignment, professional credential or permission to share private records.</p><p>Any paid or private work requires separately agreed terms before it starts.</p></section><section class="panel"><p class="tag">04 · Check the result</p><h2>Say what worked and what needs correction.</h2><p>After a scoped resource or step is provided, acknowledge receipt and give factual, structured feedback. You can request a correction without publishing a review.</p><p>Feedback remains private. Favorable feedback, volunteering and publicity are not conditions of assistance.</p></section></div><section class="section-block"><div class="callout"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your choices stay separate</p><h2>You can stop participating.</h2><p>Withdraw through your private link while it is valid. This stops this application’s active review; it does not change separate newsletter choices or erase required consent history. Contact us for access or deletion questions.</p></div><a class="button secondary" href="/community/privacy/">Understand your choices</a></div></section><section class="section-block"><h2>What this does not open</h2><p>Member discussion rooms, public profiles, matching, shared case files, public feedback and scheduled classes require separate releases. Reviewer and witness applicants need appropriate training, competence checks, conflicts review and assignment consent before taking part in real work.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/community/assistance/">Ask about support</a><a class="button secondary" href="/community/reviewers/">Apply to contribute</a><a href="/community/status/">Current service status</a></div></section>''',False)
    page('community/operate','Workshop operations','Private owner operations for applications, capacity and documented human decisions.', '''<div class="operations-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Private owner workspace</p><h1>Keep the loop moving.</h1><p class="lede">Review the next step, make a deliberate decision and preserve the person’s choices.</p></div><button id="operator-signout" class="button secondary" type="button" hidden>Sign out</button></div><p id="operator-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Sign in with your existing authorized operator account.</p><section class="panel login-panel" id="operator-login-panel"><h2>Owner sign in</h2><p>Only an existing account with current operator permission can open this queue. Community applications do not create an operator account.</p><form id="operator-login"><div class="field"><label for="operator-email">Operator email</label><input id="operator-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="username" required></div><div class="field"><label for="operator-password">Password</label><input id="operator-password" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" required></div><button type="submit">Sign in privately</button></form><p class="small">This page keeps the access token in memory only, for at most 30 minutes. Reloading signs this page out. No password or access token is placed in a link or browser storage.</p></section><div id="operator-workspace" hidden><section class="section-block"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Capacity before commitments</p><h2>Review queue</h2></div><button id="operator-refresh" class="button secondary" type="button">Refresh queue</button></div><div id="operator-capacity" class="capacity-strip"></div><p class="small" id="operator-queue-summary"></p><div class="operations-layout"><section class="panel queue-panel"><label class="field-label" for="operator-filter">Show</label><select id="operator-filter"><option value="active">Active applications</option><option value="archived">Closed or withdrawn</option><option value="all">All applications</option></select><div id="operator-queue" aria-live="polite"></div></section><section class="panel decision-panel" id="operator-detail"><h2>Select an application</h2><p>The queue contains live records only. An empty queue is shown as empty.</p></section></div></section><section class="section-block"><div class="notice"><strong>Keep commitments deliberate.</strong><br>These controls record human decisions. They do not grant tool access, credentials, charge money, schedule appointments or publish feedback. A decision does not send an email. A generic update notice requires a separate preview and explicit sending action.</div></section></div><noscript><p>JavaScript is required for this private workspace. No application information is rendered into this static page.</p></noscript>''','operations.js')
